The Salesforce Composite REST API (`/services/data/v50.0/composite/`) processes multiple subrequests in a single transaction — if any subrequest fails, the entire batch is rolled back. Subrequests are executed in order, and `@{referenceId}` resolves the saved record's ID from a prior subrequest, so the Asset can reference the Account and the trigger on Service_Request__c will find the Asset by SerialNumber.

```http
POST /services/data/v50.0/composite/ HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <access_token>

{
  "allOrNone": true,
  "subrequests": [
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "url": "/services/data/v50.0/sobjects/Account",
      "referenceId": "newAccount",
      "body": {
        "Name": "Hollis Outdoor Supply"
      }
    },
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "url": "/services/data/v50.0/sobjects/Asset",
      "referenceId": "newAsset",
      "body": {
        "Name": "Trailhead Kiosk 3000",
        "SerialNumber": "SN-88213",
        "AccountId": "@{newAccount}"
      }
    },
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "url": "/services/data/v50.0/sobjects/Service_Request__c",
      "referenceId": "newRequest",
      "body": {
        "Subject__c": "Installation",
        "Serial_Number__c": "SN-88213"
      }
    }
  ]
}
